VERDICT: needs-changes
{"verdict":"needs-changes","summary":"Re-reading the shrink path confirms rank0's objection: rows [0,top) are NOT scrollback-resident content the terminal put there — they retain the stale pre-shrink screen-resident tail, which is simultaneously redrawn at [top,visible_rows), producing on-screen duplicate lines. The PR's own reasoning (and the new test) lock in the wrong invariant.","concede":["My prior approve — I did not trace where the terminal cursor/content actually sits during the shrink; the rows [0,top) are not innocent scrollback content."],"maintain":["The draw span [top,visible_rows) and its Clear are individually correct; the defect is specifically the removal of the [0,top) clear, not the draw logic.","The scrollback-committed invariant itself (don't draw history[..scrollback_committed]) is sound and should be preserved."],"findings":[{"file":"crates/mu-solo/src/viewport.rs","line":648,"severity":"high","issue":"In the shrink branch, set_height clears only [old_y,old_y+old_height) then calls repaint_history_tail with visible_rows=new_y but a STALE scrollback_committed (=history.len()-old_y). Since new_y>old_y, start=scrollback_committed>naive_start, rows_to_draw=old_y, top=new_y-old_y. The new clear loop `top..visible_rows` skips rows [0,top). Those rows were NOT touched by the vacated-row clear (which started at old_y) and still hold the OLD screen-resident tail history[scrollback_committed..scrollback_committed+top). The same lines are then redrawn at [top,visible_rows) (row `top` draws history[scrollback_committed], identical to what row 0 still shows), so the screen now shows duplicate copies — an on-screen duplication regression on the common turn-commit (preview-collapse) path. The old `0..visible_rows` clear was correct: it blanked the region whose true content lives in native scrollback and must not be redrawn (per the scrollback-committed invariant). The PR comment's claim that [0,top) 'hold content the terminal scrolled up there' is wrong — that content is the screen-resident tail, not scrollback overflow."},{"file":"crates/mu-solo/src/viewport.rs","line":1093,"severity":"high","issue":"The new test clear_span_never_exceeds_draw_span_after_viewport_moves_down asserts (clear_lo,clear_hi)==(draw_lo,draw_hi)==(10,40), encoding the buggy invariant that the clear span must equal the draw span. The correct behavior for this case is clear=(0,40), draw=(10,40): blank the top gap (its content is in native scrollback and must not be redrawn) and draw the screen-resident tail into [top,visible_rows). The test would fail against the correct implementation, so it locks in the regression and prevents detection."}]}
